\section{Hyperparameters for experiments}
\label{app:hparams}

In our experiments, we thoroughly tested our model on various hyperparameters using the MNIST dataset. The MNIST dataset was chosen as a baseline for hyperparameter testing due to its low computational training cost.  We found that our model was very robust with respect to the hyperparameters used, consistently generating quality generations without hyperparameter tuning. Due to limited compute, only limited tests were performed on CelebA, but we hypothesize that our model would perform well with different hyperparameters than the ones used. For the choice of our 'r', we chose a rate that was large enough to allow full degradation, enabling the model to learn to predict starting from full noise. See \ref{tab:hyperparams} for our hyperparameters used.




