\subsection{Objective Function}\label{E}
\indent
 According to \eqref{mapping} and following previous works~\cite{sawhney2021exploring,you2024dgdnn,you2024multi}, we perform the trend classification for future trading days. Thus, the objective function $L$ is formulated as follows,
\begin{equation}
    L = -\frac{1}{P} \sum_{t=1}^{T} \sum_{n=1}^{N} \sum_{i=1}^{\alpha} C_{t}^{n,i} \log(\hat{C}_{t}^{n,i}).
    \label{objective}
\end{equation}
Here, $P$ denotes the training period, $C_t^{n,i} = 1$ if stock $n$ at time $t$ belongs to class $i$, where $i=0$ denotes a downward trend and $i=1$ denotes an upward trend. $\hat{C}_{t}^{n,i}$ denotes the predicted label by the model. 

