\section{Conclusion}
This paper presents a joint approach for ASR and speaker role tagging using SOT. By fine-tuning Whisper for SOT with role-specific tokens on real-world conversational datasets, we enable it to generate transcriptions with integrated speaker role labels. Experiments show this approach outperforms an SSL-based baseline. Further analysis illustrates how model size, language pretraining, encoder freezing, and context usage affect the performance. Our findings highlight Whisper's potential as a strong foundation for speaker-aware ASR under SOT, with future directions including improved contextual modeling and generalization to broader applications.
