\subsection{RAA Parameter Design}
In this section, we aim to design the parameters of the proposed RAA architecture.
For any given sULA $n$ with orientation $\eta_n$, the path angle $\phi$ that has the maximum and minimum responses  $|r(\phi,\eta_n)|$ in (\ref{steering_eff00}) can be obtained as follows.

\begin{lem}\label{lemma01}
For any given sULA $n$ with orientation $\eta_n$,
\begin{equation}\label{hu}
\begin{aligned}
  &\underset{|\phi|\leq\phi_{\text{max}}}{\text{max}}(|r(\phi,\eta_n)|)=M, \text{ and the maximum} \\
  &\text{is achieved if and only if } \phi=\eta_n.
  \end{aligned}
\end{equation}
\end{lem}
\begin{pproof}
The
 function $|H_M(x)|$ in (\ref{H_M}) achieves the maximum value 1 when $x=0,\pm2,\pm4,\cdots$.
Consequently, $|H_M(\sin(\phi-\eta_n))|$  in (\ref{steering_eff00}) achieves the maximum value 1 if and only if $\sin(\phi-\eta_n)=0$, since $\sin(\phi-\eta_n)\in[-1,1]$. Thus, $|r(\phi,\eta_n)|$ in (\ref{steering_eff00}) achieves the maximum value $M$ if and only if $\phi=\eta_n$ due to $|\phi-\eta_n|<\pi$ with $\eta_{\max}=\phi_{\max}<0.5\pi$.
 % i.e., $\underset{x}{\text{max}}(|H_M(x)|)=|H_M(0)|=1$. Thus,
%if and only if $\sin(\phi-\eta_n)=0$, i.e., $\phi=\eta_n$, the maximum value of $|r(\phi,\eta_n)|$ in (\ref{steering_eff00}) can be obtained, i.e., $\underset{\phi}{\text{max}}(|r(\phi,\eta_n)|)=M$.
    %In other words, the maximum occurs only when the path $\mathbf{p}$ is parallel to the normal vector $\mathbf{n}$ of the L-sULA.
    %Thus, the proof of Lemma \ref{lemma01} is completed.
