\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
where ``$\overset{(a)}{\approx}$'' holds from the second-order Taylor approximation.
It is found from (\ref{BWULA}) that $\phi^{\text{ULA}}_{\text{BW},n}\geq 2\arcsin\left(\frac{2}{M}\right)$, where ``='' holds if and only if  $\phi_n=0$.
In addition, the beamwidth $\phi^{\text{ULA}}_{\text{BW},n}$ increases monotonically with $|\phi_n|$, resulting in poor angular resolution for edge users.
\end{cor}

