\begin{abstract} By a direct computation,  we show that the $P_2$ interpolation of a $P_3$
  function is also a local $H^1$-projection on uniform tetrahedral meshes, i.e.,
  the difference is $H^1$-orthogonal to the  $P_2$ Lagrange basis function on the
   support patch of tetrahedra of the basis function.
Consequently, we show the $H^1$ and $L^2$ superconvergence of the $P_2$ Lagrange finite element
   on uniform tetrahedral meshes.
Using the standard 20-points Lagrange $P_3$ interpolation,  where the 20 nodes are
  exactly some $P_2$ global basis nodes, we lift the superconvergent $P_2$ finite
   element solution to a quasi-optimal $P_3$ solution on each cube. 
Numerical results confirm the theory. 
\end{abstract}



