\section{Local $H^1$-orthogonality of the $P_2$ interpolation}

We study such local $H^1$-orthogonality of the $P_2$ interpolation of $P_3$ functions in
  this section.

\begin{lemma}\label{l-d} 
Let $p\in P_3(R_1)$,   where $R_1$ is the support patch of tetrahedra of
   mid-cube node basis function $\phi_1$, cf. Figure \ref{3r1}.
    Then the $P_2$ nodal interpolation of $p$, $I_2 p$, is the local $H^1$-projection of $p$,
     i.e., 
\an{\label{d-3-1} (\nabla(p-I_2 p), \nabla \phi_1)_{R_1} = 0.  }  
 \end{lemma} 

\begin{proof}  We shift and isotropic scale the patch  $R_1$ to
  the one  shown in Figure \ref{3r1}.

