For any $t \in [0,T]$ and $k=0,\ldots, K$, applying the Taylor theorem to $\tilde{\eta}$, there exists $r_{1} \in (0,1)$ such that  
\begin{align}
& \frac{ \tilde{\eta}(t,(k + 1)\Delta x) -2\tilde{\eta}(t,k\Delta x) + \tilde{\eta}(t,(k - 1)\Delta x) }{(\Delta x)^{2}} \nonumber\\
	= & \frac{1}{2}\left\{ \partial_{x}^{2}\tilde{\eta}( t, (k + r_{1})\Delta x ) 
