\paragraph{Overall Procedure.} 
We instantiate \( N \) agents, each receiving the game rules and its assigned story only once at the beginning.

Each round begins with agents independently declaring their contribution amounts. At the end of each round, agents are informed of the group's total contribution and their individual payoff.

Depending on the experimental condition, each agent is either primed with the same story or assigned a random story from a pool of 12 stories (eight meaningful cooperation-themed narratives in pink and four baseline conditions in blue: no instruction, self-interest directives, or nonsensical stories).

After all \( R \) rounds, we evaluate both individual cumulative payoffs and total group performance.
