Figure~\ref{fig:PV} illustrates the passivity index when $K_P$ is varied for the cases of $(P_\rf,Q_\rf)=(0,0)$ and $(P_\rf,Q_\rf)=(1,0.5)$. Increasing $K_P$ boosts the passivity index without posing any risk of an increase in the zero-crossing frequency.

