\section{Conclusion}
In conclusion, the paper has developed a multimodal multi-objective optimization algorithm evaluation metric based on a Regionalized Metric Framework, addressing the current research gap. The algorithm was fully implemented in Matlab and tested using the CEC2019 test set, validating the research hypothesis. The proposed evaluation index improves objectivity by overcoming the limitations of reference sets, allowing for the assessment of convergence and diversity in optimal solution sets, aiding future algorithm improvements.

Future work will focus on refining partition evaluation rules for higher-dimensional test problems and optimizing the use of derivatives, aiming to minimize them by adopting a more general region partitioning approach.


