Each voter approves the two candidates representing her column and row. 
For the committee size $k = r$, most well-known proportional voting rules (such as PAV, MES, and sequential-Phragm\'en) select only the committee consisting of all row candidates and the committee consisting of all column candidates. However, these two committees are not connected in the respective choice sets.
