First, we claim that the committee $\{c_1,c_2,c_3\}$ satisfies EJR. For this, observe that the first three voters are fully satisfied, while the last three voters can only claim a single candidate. 
    As the latter voters approve $c_3$, they do not constitute an EJR violation. 
    Due to the symmetry of the instance, the committee $\{c_3, c_6, c_7\}$ also satisfies EJR. 
