  performance, Linear algebra}
    \strng{namehash}{LTM+1}
    \strng{fullhash}{LTMIFDSTMQOES1}
    \field{labelnamesource}{author}
    \field{labeltitlesource}{title}
    \field{sortinit}{L}
    \field{sortinithash}{L}
    \field{abstract}{%
    We show how the BLAS-like Library Instantiation Software (BLIS) framework,
  which provides a more detailed layering of the GotoBLAS (now maintained as
  OpenBLAS) implementation, allows one to analytically determine tuning
  parameters for high-end instantiations of the matrix-matrix multiplication.
  This is of both practical and scientific importance, as it greatly reduces
  the development effort required for the implementation of the level-3 BLAS
  while also advancing our understanding of how hierarchically layered memories
  interact with high-performance software. This allows the community to move on
  from valuable engineering solutions (empirically autotuning) to scientific
  understanding (analytical insight).%
    }
