\newcommand{\mh}{\textsc{m}\mu}
\newcommand{\hm}{\textsc{hm}}
\newcommand{\hh}{\textsc{h}\mu}
\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{cccc}
$6\times8 (\mm)$ & $6\times4 (\hm)$ & $6\times2 (\hm)$ & $6\times1 (\hm)$ \\
$4\times8 (\mh)$ & $4\times4 (\hh)$ & $4\times2 (\hh)$ & $4\times1 (\hh)$ \\
$2\times8 (\mh)$ & $2\times4 (\hh)$ & $2\times2 (\hh)$ & $2\times1 (\hh)$ \\
$1\times8 (\mh)$ & $1\times4 (\hh)$ & $1\times2 (\hh)$ & $1\times1 (\hh)$
\end{tabular}
\end{center}
Here, $\mm$ denotes the main millikernel that is called from the 2nd loop, and $\mh$ denotes its helper microkernels. Similarly, the $\hm$ labels denote helper millikernels, each of which calls its own helper microkernels labeled by $\hh$.


