\section{Conclusions}

Developing this filesystem driver needed a special attention to, firstly, the filesystem on-disk layout, then to U-Boot's architecture. It showed how the project's constraints change when it is cross-compiled and when tests are run with bigger SquashFS images.

The personal ideas of coding style and software engineering must be set aside when contributing to an Open Source project, because the project already has its own coding style and architecture to be respected.

