The merit of using additive synthesis is visualized in Figure \ref{fig:AS_visual}. Compared to the left spectrogram produced without AS, the right spectrogram with AS produces visibly more harmonics. Further these harmonics are more stable and outstanding from their frequency neighbors. Perceptually, this reduces the dullness of the output. Further, it is not difficult to notice lots of horizontal noise lines between harmonics and at the bottom of the spectrogram. With the harmonics information, model's predictions in these area either get eliminated or better align with the harmonics, which consequently reduces the ringing sounds in the audio.

