\section{Conclusion}

We propose two techniques to respectively utilize the two observations for improving the concatenative singing voice conversion performance. The use of additive synthesis allows the model the capture fine harmonic details, and consequently produces clearer output. Our concatenation smoothness optimization at inference time introduces candidates and summing weights that align better with their temporal neighbors, reducing enhancement stress on the vocoder model and thus producing smoother output. Empirically, while the autoregressive reselection process represents an unavoidable trade-off between local accuracy and temporal smoothness, one can always adjust the the multiplier coefficient to achieve the desirable balance. We regard these two techniques as decent improvements on concatenative singing voice conversion models.

