\subsection{Analysis Approach}

Based on relevance of actions to the immediate state of the chat with the agent,
we interpret the presence and ordering of codes on participant actions at the prompt level (e.g., verifying code changes, stopping the agent) or at the issue level (e.g., writing code, running tests) and analyze codes on chat interactions at the prompt level. Since participants were instructed to think aloud, we do not analyze the durations of their activities, nor do we analyze the absolute counts of these activities to avoid biases toward participants who performed actions repetitively in shorter intervals. We also note specific utterances and scenarios that indicate communication barriers, reporting only those that recur across different participants.


While our results are largely qualitative,
we include some numerical data throughout to give the reader
a fuller sense of the trends that we observed.
However, given the exploratory nature of the study and the 
relatively small sample sizes, we caution the reader against
broad extrapolation or generalization.
Congruently, we present findings descriptively, 
without applying inferential statistics.

Towards helping to ensure the validity of our findings, 
we sent an early version of our 
results to all participants as a member check~\cite{motulsky2021member}.
Our study protocol has undergone privacy assessment and review by
our organization.
To aid in replication,
qualitative codebooks and 
study materials can be accessed in our Supplementary Material.
