\subsection{RQ2: Developer-Agent Communication Barriers}


\subsubsection{Lack of tacit knowledge} \label{tacit}
The agent was sometimes an ineffective collaborator 
because it lacked \textit{tacit} knowledge,
a type of knowledge that is gained through personal experience, 
rather than through explicit documentation.
Rus and Lindvall~\cite{Rus_tacitk} show that tacit knowledge 
comprises the majority of software engineering knowledge. 
The lack of such knowledge can make it difficult for new 
collaborators (such as the agent) to work effectively 
as they lack the knowledge that developers who are experienced 
with the repository, such as the participant, may have. 
Further, unlike expert insights into implementation details, 
it is difficult for the agent to learn tacit knowledge, 
as it is difficult to know when and how to communicate such information.
