\subsubsection{Ineffective Follow-Up Suggestions} \label{sec:followup}
The agent offered textual suggestions for follow-up prompts 
in 62\% of its responses.
% , like the one marked by (d) in Figure~\ref{fig:workflow}.
% that starts with ``Would you like me to make any adjustments...?"
These suggestions were usually 
not effective in advancing the conversation--  participants replied to only 7\% of such follow ups 
in their next prompt. 
One reason for this may be that these suggestions were often 
non-specific (e.g.:  Figure~\ref{fig:workflow}d).
When participants did reply, the suggestions were more 
specific (e.g.: \textit{Would you like me to show you how to 
remove the manual tracking code and let RichEdit handle double-clicks naively?}).
Further, while participants often needed refinements 
to code changes, the agent's follow ups instead would often suggest 
moving forward to other steps in the issue resolution process. 
Thus, participants may also not have 
responded to follow ups because they
did not always reflect the true state of the solution.


