\subsubsection{External Factors}\label{priorsuccess}
Participants' success was influenced by external factors relating to the tool and the task, such as prior experience and nature of the issue. The 3 participants with previous experience with Cursor had more success (3 out of 4 issues resolved), compared to others' 52\% (13 out of 25) success-rate.


Participants were most successful solving bugs that only 
concerned user interface changes (5 out of 5 issues resolved), 
followed by refactoring/variable renaming issues (2 out of 3 issues resolved), 
then feature requests (4 out of 8 issues resolved), 
and finally bugs (5 out of 13 issues resolved). 
These results suggest that participants may have struggled to 
collaborate with the agent on non-code generation tasks such as localization and debugging
that are critical to 
bug resolution.

