\section{Conclusion}
In this paper, we've seen that developers can collaborate with 
a SWE agent to solve real-world software engineering
tasks, but also that such a collaboration is fraught
and that success is not guaranteed.
While the capabilities of large language models and of the 
agents that build upon them expands at a dizzying rate, 
the capabilities of the humans who work with them are relatively
static.
The strategies, challenges, and communication patterns we 
document here are therefore likely to remain relevant even as 
SWE agents rapidly evolve. 
By understanding and addressing these enduring human factors, 
we hope this work contributes to a future where developer-agent collaboration is both effective and empowering.


