\begin{abstract}
The Riemann zeta function, and more generally the $L$-functions of Dirichlet characters, are among the central objects of study in analytic number theory. We report on a project to formalize the theory of these objects in Lean's `Mathlib' library, including a proof of Dirichlet's theorem on primes in arithmetic progressions and a formal statement of the Riemann hypothesis.
\end{abstract}

